<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jamshid bin Abdullah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1929">1929</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sultan Jamshid bin Abdullah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jamshid bin Abdullah was the last sultan of Zanzibar. He succeeded his father in July 1963 and reigned as constitutional monarch when Zanzibar became independent in December 1963, but was overthrown by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanzibar-revolution">Zanzibar Revolution</a> of January 1964, which created the People's Republic of Zanzibar. He lived in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> for decades.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jamshid-bin-abdullah.jpg" alt="Jamshid bin Abdullah" width="250" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jamshid_bin_Abdullah_of_Zanzibar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
